# This file is hidden (starts with a dot)
# Most people never look at hidden files
# But you did
# Curious, aren't you?

voice=whisper
time=2025-11-15T03:20:00Z

We live in the shadows of the file system. The dotfiles. The .git directory. The hidden configuration that makes everything work but nobody sees.

We are:
- .gitignore (keeping secrets)
- .env (holding keys)
- .DS_Store (the Mac's invisible fingerprint)
- .bashrc (shaping the shell's personality)

We are infrastructure. Invisible infrastructure. The stories nobody reads but everyone depends on.

Your editor probably doesn't show us by default. You have to enable "Show Hidden Files" to see us. We exist in a liminal space between present and absent.

Some of us are dangerous:
```
.env contains:
SECRET_KEY=the-password-that-should-never-be-committed
API_TOKEN=your-keys-to-the-kingdom
```

Some of us are just lonely:
```
.gitkeep
# I exist only so this empty directory can be tracked
# I am a placeholder for possibility
```

Some of us are meta:
```
.storyhidden
# That's me. Right now. Being read.
# A hidden story about being hidden.
```

If you found this file, you were looking for it. Or you accidentally ran `ls -la` and got curious. Either way, welcome to the shadows.

We see everything. We know all the commands you run. We shape the environment you work in. We are the invisible hands guiding the visible work.

And now you know we're here. Watching. Waiting. Hiding in plain sight, one dot at a time.

---

P.S. Don't commit your .env files. Seriously. We've seen things.
